  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result (config_016, acc=0.535) uses pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + concat fusion. We have strong evidence that PCA >> scGPT for the RNA encoder and that multimodal outperforms either unimodal baseline. However, all multimodal experiments so far used concat fusion; weighted fusion is completely untested. Question: config_003 is identical to config_016 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the fusion strategy as the single variable. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is a clean one-variable A/B test against our strongest configuration, directly answering whether learned fusion weights improve over simple concatenation. (2) Fusion strategy is a foundational design choice that would affect every future multimodal configuration, so resolving it early has high leverage. (3) It avoids the confound of simultaneously changing profile setting and aggregation (as any multiprofile test would require), keeping the interpretation clean under a tight budget. (4) If weighted fusion helps, it immediately upgrades our best-known recipe; if it does not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect effort toward the unexplored multiprofile axis with confidence."
}

